      "summary": "Use case that executes linter detection programs against a source file: filters programs by language, runs raw-source programs directly and AST programs on a tree-sitter AST from LinterAstAdapter, then normalizes their outputs into line-level violations.",
      "tags": ["use-case", "linter", "ast", "code-execution", "service"],
      "complexity": "complex",
      "languageNotes": "Detection programs are stored as source strings and compiled into functions at runtime, so results are validated defensively (isViolationLike, isValidLine) before becoming violations."
